  "title": "Porsche’s Transaxle Experiment Turns 50",
  "summary": "It’s 50 years since Porsche did the unthinkable. The company, built on rear-engined sports cars, decided to put a motor up front instead. The Porsche 924, which arrived in 1976, wasn’t even originally a Porsche, but it did lead the company in a whole new direction—one which could have killed off the 911 completely. The […]",
